'' A PROGRAM NAMES WHAT ITS MODULES EXPORT (ADR 0017; RFC-0002 §2, RFC-0004 §4-5). Each
'' module, compiled in order, leaves its interface; each '#import' reads it in, after the
'' interfaces it depends on and each once -- main imports esc and http, and http imports
'' esc, so esc's is read once and its Url is one type. Through the alias, through 'as',
'' through 'using': a function whose signature names another module's type through that
'' module's own alias, a generic instantiated in the program whose body calls a module-private helper, a const, an enum, a namespace
'' member, two shared variables (one written by http and read by main) and esc's public
'' 'operator +', found with no 'using'. Every name links by the module's chain, so the
'' program runs; and '#ifdef Quote' in main stays false, since an interface's names are
'' not the importer's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/iface/libs tests/modules/src/iface/app/main.bas -o tests/modules/ifacelink.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/modules/ifacelink.exe
'' RUN: tests/modules/ifacelink.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: <a>
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: <a><a>
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  80
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: <bc> 2
